  "generated_text": "Let the other endpoint be $(x, y)$. The midpoint formula gives us:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{4+x}{2}, \\frac{3+y}{2}\\right) = (2,9)\n\\]\nFrom this, we get two equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{4+x}{2} &= 2 \\\\\n\\frac{3+y}{2} &= 9\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nSolving these equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n4+x &= 4 \\\\\n3+y &= 18\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= 0 \\\\\ny &= 15\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\nThus, the other endpoint is $(0,15)$. The sum of its coordinates is $0 + 15 = \\boxed{15}$.",
